## MULTIPLE CANDIDATE MEMORIES

One analysis can generate multiple memories.

Example:

Developer statement:

"We originally used a file-based bridge because the WebSocket connection was unreliable on some trader home networks."

Possible extracted memories:

Memory 1:
Decision:
Used file-based bridge.

Reason:
WebSocket reliability problems.

Memory 2:
Historical experiment:
Previously implemented WebSocket bridge.

Outcome:
Persistent connections were unreliable under some network conditions.

Memory 3:
Affected component:
External trader bridge.

The confirmation should apply to the complete candidate set unless the user selects individual memories.

