## CRITICAL CONSISTENCY REQUIREMENT

Kassandra's displayed answer must match the actual Sibyl database.

Never display:

"Confirmed by institutional memory"

unless the memory actually exists in Sibyl and has:

source = developer or verified human source
confidence = confirmed
status = stored

Never display:

"Verified from institutional memory"

when the information only came from inference.

Never display a successful save confirmation unless the database write succeeded.

The UI and database must agree.

---

## POST-SAVE VERIFICATION

After saving memories, perform a read-back verification.

Example:

saved_memories = save_to_sibyl(candidate_memories)

verified_memories = get_memories_by_ids(saved_memories.ids)

IF verified_memories count != saved_memories count:
report storage failure
do not claim successful save

ELSE:
return success response with actual stored memory IDs/count

This prevents phantom memory saves.

