## IMPORTANT: SEPARATE CANDIDATE FROM PERMANENT MEMORY

Use two concepts:

CANDIDATE MEMORY

Temporary.
Can be wrong.
Can be edited.
Awaiting confirmation.

PERMANENT SIBYL MEMORY

Stored.
Has provenance.
Has confidence.
Can be retrieved by Kassandra.

Do not place unconfirmed candidates into permanent institutional memory.

Do not lose candidates when asking the user for confirmation.

